---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import RothVsTraditionalCalculator from '../../components/RothVsTraditionalCalculator';
---

<Layout
  title="Roth vs. Traditional Calculator"
  description="Free calculator comparing estimated after-tax retirement outcomes between Roth and Traditional contributions, based on your current and expected future tax rate."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-brand">Tool<span class="text-orange">/</span></p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-paper sm:text-4xl">Roth vs. Traditional Calculator</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-muted">
      See an estimated after-tax comparison based on your current tax rate and what you expect it to be in retirement.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8">
      <RothVsTraditionalCalculator client:load />
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert mt-10 max-w-none prose-a:text-brand">
      <h2>How this calculator works</h2>
      <p>
        This tool compares contributions that have the <em>same impact on your take-home pay today</em> — since a
        Traditional contribution is tax-deductible now and a Roth contribution isn't, an equal dollar amount isn't
        actually a fair comparison. The calculator adjusts the Roth contribution down to match the same after-tax
        cost, then projects both forward and applies tax only to the Traditional balance at withdrawal.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read our full <a href="/blog/roth-ira-vs-traditional-ira/">Roth vs. Traditional IRA guide</a> for the
        reasoning behind this trade-off in more depth, or compare workplace and personal Roth accounts in our
        <a href="/blog/roth-401k-vs-roth-ira/">Roth 401(k) vs. Roth IRA</a> guide.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
